{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "סקול יסקל", :translit "yisakel sokel", :gloss "shall be stoned, stoned"} {:he "סקול יסקל השור", :translit "yisakel sokel hashor", :gloss "shall be stoned, the ox shall be stoned"} {:he "דילפינן לדורות מכאן", :translit "dilfinan l'dorot mikan", :gloss "we learn for generations from here"} {:he "מה כאן בדחייה ובסקילה אף לדורות דחייה וסקילה", :translit "mah kan bid'chiyah uviskilah af l'dorot d'chiyah v'skilah", :gloss "what here by pushing away and by stoning, so for generations pushing away and stoning"} {:he "אם בהמה אם איש לא יחיה", :translit "im behemah im ish lo yichyeh", :gloss "if beast or man, he shall not live"} {:he "בקללה מתחילין מן הקטן", :translit "b'kelalah matchilin min hakatan", :gloss "in cursing one begins from the small"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["סקול יסקל" "סקול יסקל השור"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase \"סקול יסקל השור\" appears in Exodus 21:28 regarding the ox that kills a person. The Talmud derives that stoning of an animal is preceded by pushing it over a cliff (דחייה), learning the procedure for all generations from Sinai (Sanhedrin 78b). The phrase \"בקללה מתחילין מן הקטן\" is a Talmudic principle found in Shabbat 105b.", :sources ["Exodus 21:28" "Sanhedrin 78b" "Shabbat 105b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "במשך", :translit "bamshoch", :gloss "when drawn out"} {:he "במשוך בקרן היובל", :translit "bamshoch b'karen hayovel", :gloss "when drawing out with the horn of the jubilee"} {:he "שופר מאילו של יצחק", :translit "shofar me'eilu shel yitzchak", :gloss "a shofar from the ram of Isaac"} {:he "ובזכות זה השופר של מתן תורה נפלה חומת יריחו", :translit "uvizchut zeh hashofar shel mattan torah naflah chomat yericho", :gloss "and in the merit of this shofar of the giving of Torah fell the wall of Jericho"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["במשך" "במשוך בקרן היובל"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase \"במשוך בקרן היובל\" appears in Joshua 6:5, 6:20 in the context of the battle of Jericho. The Talmud identifies the shofar at Sinai as coming from the ram sacrificed in place of Isaac (Genesis 22:13), as stated in Shabbat 82b. The Ram of Isaac is the ram whose horns were created for specific redemptive moments, as taught in Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 31 and Avodah Zarah 5a.", :sources ["Joshua 6:5" "Joshua 6:20" "Genesis 22:13" "Shabbat 82b" "Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 31" "Avodah Zarah 5a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["סקול יסקל" "סקול יסקל השור"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "סקול יסקל", :refs ["Exodus 19:13" "Exodus 21:28"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "סקול יסקל השור", :refs ["Exodus 21:28"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["במשך" "במשוך בקרן היובל"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "במשך", :refs ["Exodus 19:13" "Joshua 6:5" "Amos 9:13"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "במשוך בקרן היובל", :refs ["Joshua 6:5"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:32.844637009Z", :model "glm-5.2"}